# T8 is touched at ~310.5 s; its killer-scene chain holds the player controller ~13 s, so the
# killer approach starts after the handback. TouchTrigger7 (tueur_conducteur, r850 at
# 1093,-13854) fires earlier on the shore walk (~289.6 s) - that is the game's own chain.

# ---- the killer: the walked T7 shore touch (~289.6 s) sends the killer to the parking wall;
# he parks at ~(1771,-13026) (measured with track, scratch item30c_e3/e5/e6). The north firing
# pose and a 372 UU southern spot deal zero damage (the wall blocks; measured), so the player
# walks down the proven nav legs after the T8 handback (~13 s scene hold) and fights from
# (1771,-13200), 174 UU south of him. The killer walks while attacking, so the view is tracked
# onto it. `equip` re-selects the picked-up Beretta: the scripted T8 scene had left `Fists`
# selected (measured: without it the fires were fist swings - weapon Fists3, bone None).
